TheRegExp.escape()method returns string where characters that belongs
to the regular expression syntax are escaped.

This makes it possible to treat characters like +, *, ?, ^, $, (, ), [, ], {, }, |, and \ literally,
and not as part of a regular expression.

RegExp.escape()is an ECMAScript 2025 feature.

JavaScript 2025is fully supported in all modern browsers sinceMay 2025:

